    'Four representative directions, to make this concrete. Segmentation: partition components or decisions behind a stable interface. Local Quality: assign context-specific behaviour under a declared context. Prior Action: prepare reusable state before the critical path. Parameter Change: adjust a type, a threshold, a loss, a weight, or an operating point. The full forty-class map is in Appendix B. But please note the scope: the experiments evaluate selected instances, not all forty principles across all tasks. We are not claiming that the map has been validated end to end.',
