    # 10
    "Functional information is where we are most often misunderstood, so let me be precise. It is not a population-independent measure of quality. At a given evidence level, take a reference set of configurations evaluated under the same protocol and the same qualification rules. Useful FI is minus log base two of the fraction that reach the candidate's useful level. Harm FI is the same construction over harm measures: false positive rate, recall loss, leakage, resource violations. The add-one correction keeps the estimate finite when nothing matches. It is not a confidence guarantee.",
    # 11
    'Ideality combines the two conservatively: the lower bound on useful FI over the upper bound on harm FI plus a path-cost term. Certification is a separate quantity, the highest evidence level whose validation requirements and hard gates were actually passed, or minus one if none were. Two cautions. Mandatory integrity, safety, replication and resource checks cannot be compensated by a larger ratio. And this equation is a method specification: our historical runs use harm point estimates, and the campaign uses construction steps over six as a cost proxy, not measured runtime or energy.',
